nevada state police are still not  answering questions about a tragic  accident that happened nearly two weeks  ago but the 8 news now i-team is  uncovering new information metro police  detective justin terry was killed after  a beam collapsed on the car he was  driving the i-team's vanessa murphy  obtained new documents which may help  provide insight about what exactly  happened  yeah we're trying to put the pieces  together here about what happened and  it's a challenge since nevada state  police are not providing answers but we  now have the permits for the company  which owns the truck involved metro  police detective justin terry was  driving near the centennial bowl project  on the morning of june 10th when a  tractor-trailer hit an early warning  beam for a bridge up ahead the beam  collapsed on terry's car and he died at  the scene the 8 news now i-team learned  north las vegas-based western states  contracting is responsible for that  truck according to the nevada department  of transportation the company had  10 ndot issued permits at the time of  the accident all of them for a truck 15  feet high an ndot spokesman says the  beam is  at least 15 feet high so you can see how  it didn't make it under the permits also  specify only one piece of freight is  allowed when overweight is involved a  pilot car is required and there are also  route restrictions without additional  information though it's difficult to  determine whether rules were violated  i'm also waiting to find out if nevada  state police have determined whether  that beam was properly secured back to  you
 

